## Audit — remaining integrity (code only)

Date: 2026-09-15
HEAD at start: 1e37730b
Worktree: /home/nw-kirill/neuro-workflow-pr88
Branch: feat/two-jupyter-spaces-review (tracks origin/feat/two-jupyter-spaces)

Carlos/Kirill product already matches on GitHub (b0fd516e): project/community
aliases, owner Open/Close, review as label, NODE_PUBLISH_REQUIRES_REVIEW off.
This pass is Gate A (audit harden), not new product.

Match matrix
------------
- Canonical project/community; aliases internal/hackathon; groups nw-internal /
  nw-hackathon; project wins if both; exact-match rejects nw-internal-mentees.
- Hub defaults internal/hackathon; disk codes-community/ else codes-hackathon/.
- Owner publish; review_status; 0005/0006 untouched.
- Operator cutover (Keycloak rename, Hub users project/community, mv
  codes-hackathon) stays listed, not executed.

Findings this pass will fix
---------------------------
1. Hash uniqueness + catalog sync used exact tenant= and missed leftover
   internal/hackathon slugs (unique (file_hash, tenant) collision at migrate).
2. Copy constructors wrote FileField into project MEDIA_ROOT; community copies
   could be ingested by Sync as public project catalog.
3. Reviewer POST /publish/ still opened in_review nodes. make_public was
   bool(value) so "false" was True. Reject lacked self-review block.
4. jupyterhub_config _hub_tenant ignored JUPYTERHUB_*_USER. Execution service
   defaulted to JUPYTER_EXECUTION_USER, not hub_username_for_tenant. Prod
   compose missing those knobs.
5. Serializers emitted raw DB tenant; homeView list did not normalizeTenant;
   owner-reviewer still saw Approve/Reject.

Non-goals (unchanged)
---------------------
No merge, no deploy, no /data writes, no sudo, no Hub recreate, no Keycloak
admin, no review-queue page, no rewrite of 0007/0008, no raising on unknown
tenant. Implement/deploy runbook stays internal (control workspace only).

This pass does not deploy.

